                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Its trailer is promising, but the game does not deliver on those promises. Online play is not even available despite being talked about in news updates for a while as if it exists. The local split screen version of the game is still nice in my opinion, but I would like to see more to do with better UI design and smarter controls for keyboard and controller alike. I hate that the main menu doesn't use the joystick to select menu items, instead using it to rotate the not-so-interesting hockey puck-like character in the middle of the screen. Not intuitive, guys.\n\nThere are tons of glitches. I got stuck in the floor at least 3 times in the 15 minutes I played, and I wasn't doing anything that should ever result in getting stuck. I was just moving forward or running in a circle, strafing around the enemy. One time, I grazed the side of a ramp and got stuck on it, unable to move at all. All other times, I just got stuck in the middle of combat, unable to do anything other than fire my weapon.\n\nOverall, it's just a hot mess of terrible design decisions and disappointingly slow and uninteresting combat with way too many glitches. I hope the devs really take the criticism well and build on this game's current state to make it more of a polished experience with faster action and intuitive controls.",
